<Base page="privacy" title="Privacy Policy | Wizardlenz XR Studio" description="How Wizardlenz XR Studio (OPC) Private Limited collects, uses, shares and protects personal data, and the rights you have over it.">
<div class="view"><section class="pg-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="crumb"><a href="/" data-portal="Home">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</p><h1 class="pg-h1">Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lead">What we collect, why we collect it, who we share it with, how long we keep it and the rights you have, written to follow Indian data-protection law.</p><p class="ld-meta"><span>Effective date: 12 November 2026</span><span>Last updated: 12 November 2026</span><span>Wizardlenz XR Studio (OPC) Private Limited</span></p></div></section>
<section class="ld"><div class="wrap ld-grid">
<nav class="ld-toc" aria-label="On this page"><p class="ld-toc-h">On this page</p><ol><li><a href="#s1">Introduction</a></li><li><a href="#s2">Information we collect</a></li><li><a href="#s3">How the contact form works</a></li><li><a href="#s4">Why we use your information</a></li><li><a href="#s5">Lawful basis and consent</a></li><li><a href="#s6">Who we share information with</a></li><li><a href="#s7">Transfers outside India</a></li><li><a href="#s8">How long we keep information</a></li><li><a href="#s9">Security</a></li><li><a href="#s10">Photographs, video and gallery</a></li><li><a href="#s11">Children</a></li><li><a href="#s12">Your rights</a></li><li><a href="#s13">Third-party links</a></li><li><a href="#s14">Changes to this Policy</a></li><li><a href="#s15">Grievance Officer and contact</a></li></ol></nav>
<article class="ld-doc">

<div class="ld-sec" id="s1"><h2><span>1</span>Introduction</h2><p>Wizardlenz XR Studio (OPC) Private Limited (“<b>Wizardlenz</b>”, “<b>we</b>”, “<b>us</b>”) respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what personal data we collect through www.wizardlenzxrstudio.com (the “<b>Website</b>”) and in the course of our Academy, Studio and Originals services, why we collect it, how we use and protect it, and the choices and rights you have.</p><p>It is written to meet the requirements of the Information Technology Act, 2000, the Information Technology (Reasonable Security Practices and Procedures and Sensitive Personal Data or Information) Rules, 2011, and the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (together, “<b>Indian Data Protection Law</b>”). For the personal data described in this Policy, we act as the data fiduciary (controller) unless we state otherwise.</p><p>By using the Website or giving us your information, you acknowledge this Policy. Where the law requires your consent, we will ask for it clearly, and you may withdraw it at any time.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s2"><h2><span>2</span>Information we collect</h2><p>We keep collection to what we need.</p><h3>Information you give us</h3><ul><li><b>Enquiry details:</b> your name, organisation, email address, phone number, the type of enquirer (institution, business, developer or partner) and the message you write.</li><li><b>Correspondence:</b> emails, calls, meeting notes, proposals and feedback exchanged with us.</li><li><b>Programme and project information:</b> for Academy programmes (XR and AI), participant lists, attendance and assessment records, and certificate details, usually supplied by the institution or organisation that engages us; for Studio projects, business contacts and the materials you provide for the work.</li><li><b>Payment records:</b> invoices, GST details and proof of payment. We do not collect or store card or bank login details on the Website.</li><li><b>AI programme activity:</b> where an Academy AI programme uses third-party AI tools, prompts and files that participants enter are handled by those providers under their own privacy terms. We advise participants not to enter personal, confidential or sensitive data, and we do not use participants’ prompts to train AI models.</li><li><b>Photographs and video:</b> images or recordings taken at workshops and events, as described in section 10.</li></ul><h3>Information collected automatically</h3><ul><li><b>Technical data</b> handled by our hosting and network providers when you visit: IP address, browser type, device, pages requested and timestamps, kept in server logs for security and reliability.</li><li><b>Browser storage:</b> the Website uses your browser’s session storage to remember small preferences, for example that you dismissed a chat tip, so it is not shown repeatedly. It is not used to identify you or track you across sites.</li><li><b>Fonts:</b> the Website loads typefaces from Google Fonts, so your IP address and browser details are sent to Google when a page loads.</li></ul><h3>The chat assistant</h3><p>The Wizardlenz chat assistant answers questions using information built into the Website and runs in your browser. The text you type is not sent to a server or stored by us. If you choose to follow a link or contact us from it, the information you then provide is handled as described in this Policy.</p><h3>What we do not collect</h3><p>We do not run advertising or behavioural-tracking cookies, we do not sell personal data, and we do not knowingly collect sensitive personal data such as financial account passwords, health records or biometric data through the Website.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s3"><h2><span>3</span>How the contact form works</h2><p>When you complete the contact form, the Website prepares an email addressed to <a href="mailto:inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com">inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com</a> in your own email application. Nothing is transmitted to us until you review the message and press Send in your email application. The information then reaches us through your email provider and ours.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s4"><h2><span>4</span>Why we use your information</h2><ul><li>to respond to enquiries and prepare proposals, quotations and programme plans;</li><li>to deliver, manage and support Academy programmes, Studio projects and Originals products, including issuing certificates;</li><li>to invoice, collect payment and meet accounting, tax and legal obligations;</li><li>to communicate about services you requested, schedule changes, support and important updates;</li><li>to maintain the security, integrity and performance of the Website and prevent misuse or fraud;</li><li>to improve our programmes, products and Website using feedback and aggregated information;</li><li>to showcase our work, with your permission where it identifies you or your organisation; and</li><li>to establish, exercise or defend legal claims and comply with law.</li></ul><p>We do not use your personal data for automated decisions that have legal or similarly significant effects on you.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s5"><h2><span>5</span>Lawful basis and consent</h2><p>We process personal data where you have given consent (for example when you voluntarily send an enquiry or agree to be photographed), where it is necessary to perform a contract or take steps you request, where the law allows processing for specified legitimate uses (such as responding to your own request or complying with a legal obligation), and for our legitimate business interests where permitted. You can withdraw consent at any time by writing to us; withdrawal does not affect processing already done, and we may still keep records the law requires.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s6"><h2><span>6</span>Who we share information with</h2><p>We do not sell or rent your personal data. We share it only as needed and only with:</p><ul><li><b>Service providers</b> who help us run the Website and our business, such as web hosting and content delivery, email and productivity tools, cloud storage and the Google services used for our gallery and administration, accounting and payment-processing partners. They may process data only on our instructions and under confidentiality and security obligations.</li><li><b>Your institution or organisation</b> and its authorised representatives, where we deliver a programme or project for them (for example, attendance and certificate lists).</li><li><b>Professional advisers</b> such as auditors, lawyers and insurers, under duties of confidentiality.</li><li><b>Authorities</b> where required by law, court order or a lawful request, or to protect rights, safety and security.</li><li><b>A successor</b> in the event of a merger, acquisition or restructuring, subject to this Policy continuing to protect your data.</li></ul></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s7"><h2><span>7</span>Transfers outside India</h2><p>Some of our providers (for example Google) process data on servers outside India. Where we transfer personal data abroad, we do so only as permitted by Indian Data Protection Law and take reasonable steps, such as contractual safeguards, to protect it to a comparable standard.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s8"><h2><span>8</span>How long we keep information</h2><p>We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purposes above and as the law requires. As a guide: enquiries that do not lead to engagement are kept for up to 24 months; programme, project and certificate records for the duration of the engagement and up to 7 years afterwards; and accounting and tax records for the period required under applicable law. When no longer needed, data is deleted or anonymised.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s9"><h2><span>9</span>Security</h2><p>We apply reasonable technical and organisational safeguards appropriate to the nature of the data, including encrypted connections (HTTPS), access controls on administration functions, least-privilege access for personnel and vendor due diligence. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security. If a personal data breach occurs that is likely to affect you, we will notify you and the Data Protection Board of India as required by law.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s10"><h2><span>10</span>Photographs, video and gallery</h2><p>We photograph and film workshops and events to document our work. Where we intend to publish images in which you are identifiable, we will inform you at the event or through the organiser and publish only with your consent, or that of a parent or guardian for minors. You may ask us to remove an image of you from the Website or our channels by writing to us, and we will do so within a reasonable time.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s11"><h2><span>11</span>Children</h2><p>Our Website is not directed at children under 18. We process the personal data of a child only with the verifiable consent of a parent or lawful guardian (usually obtained through the school or college organising the programme), and we do not track, monitor the behaviour of, or target advertising at children.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s12"><h2><span>12</span>Your rights</h2><p>Subject to applicable law, you have the right to:</p><ul><li>obtain confirmation of the personal data we process about you and a summary of how it is used;</li><li>request correction, completion and updating of inaccurate or incomplete data;</li><li>request erasure of personal data that is no longer necessary for its purpose, unless we must retain it by law;</li><li>withdraw your consent at any time;</li><li>nominate another person to exercise your rights if you die or become incapacitated; and</li><li>have your grievance redressed, and, if unsatisfied, complain to the Data Protection Board of India.</li></ul><p>To exercise these rights, email <a href="mailto:inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com">inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com</a> from the address we hold for you. We may need to verify your identity, and we aim to respond within 30 days.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s13"><h2><span>13</span>Third-party links</h2><p>The Website links to external sites and services (for example itch.io, social networks and partner institutions). They have their own privacy practices that we do not control. Please read their policies before sharing personal data with them.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s14"><h2><span>14</span>Changes to this Policy</h2><p>We may update this Policy to reflect changes in our practices or the law. We will post the revised version here with a new “Last updated” date and, for material changes, give more prominent notice. Please review it periodically.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s15"><h2><span>15</span>Grievance Officer and contact</h2><p>For questions, requests or complaints about this Policy or your personal data, contact the Grievance Officer, Wizardlenz XR Studio (OPC) Private Limited (registered office: Madurai, Tamil Nadu; operations: Chennai, Tamil Nadu), India. Email: <a href="mailto:inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com">inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com</a> (subject line: “Privacy”). We will acknowledge your request within 48 hours and aim to resolve it within 30 days.</p></div>

<p class="ld-end">Questions about this document? Write to <a href="mailto:inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com">inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com</a>.</p>
</article></div></section></div>
</Base>
